    "done_when": "Carry out followup f-cfs-vectorize-booking on converged-forward-solve (lead ruling c-s21-moment-space-ruling). nova.equilibrium.current.book books cells in a sequential jax.lax.scan with unroll 1 (current.py:272). On the H200 that costs 0.9, 2.8 and 8.1 s per step at 2,000, 5,000 and 10,000 cells, so it is the bottleneck of the hot path: every solve iteration does read, book and map.\n\nDone when:\n(1) The booking is vectorised over cells, by vmap over the cell and fragment batch with the per-cell work padded to a fixed fragment budget, or an equivalent. It stays one compiled program, and no Python loop or sequential scan over cells remains on the path.\n(2) Identity. The booked moments equal the scan's to roundoff (max abs and relative difference reported) at about 2,000, 5,000 and 10,000 cells, limited and diverted, on analytic states and on one-Picard-image states.\n(3) Cost. Report the per-step booking wall on the H200 at each rung, before and after, plus compile seconds and peak device memory.\n(4) Autograd. jax.jvp of the booked moments with respect to the fragment geometry, or to the inputs book receives from the read, is finite and matches central finite differences to the expected order. This is the precondition for the moment-space Newton.\n(5) tests/test_current_book_fragments.py and every test file that imports current pass by delta against base, one fresh process per file. Six ids in test_current_book_fragments.py already fail at base: list them. Add an identity test against the scan, kept as a reference function in the test, and a negative control: a padded fragment counted twice turns it red by id.\n(6) Write the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/vectorize-booking.html with plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve; reckon audit-doc must report 0 errors.\nWrite only nova/equilibrium/current.py, tests for it, and the fragment. The moment-space Newton node owns forward.py, forward_operator.py, gs.py, support_read.py and topology.py.\n\nRun conditions: H200 rows run as one job through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path in the run directory) --wait -- (targets), or one sbatch job on --partition=betelgeuse --reservation=gpu_0003_grpA --gres=gpu:1 with rungs as rows inside the allocation (never an array), --time sized to finish, XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false and TMPDIR=/tmp in the submit environment and in every child; submit for real and read squeue a minute later rather than trusting sbatch --test-only. On a compute node run /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree and never invoke uv; every login-node uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. Gates pass by delta against orientation_base_sha in per-module fresh processes, both arms running the same test files with the repository root conftest, baseline_suite and after_suite as single-line JSON whose log_path names one log file and whose command is literally runnable. Any wait is declared on the job that finishes last as wait_probe [\"sacct\",\"-n\",\"-X\",\"-P\",\"-j\",\"(job id)\",\"-o\",\"State\"] and wait_terminal [\"COMPLETED\",\"FAILED\",\"CANCELLED\",\"TIMEOUT\",\"OUT_OF_MEMORY\",\"NODE_FAIL\"] as JSON lists, and names every job it depends on in wait_condition. The certified 550, 2,000 and 5,000-cell machines and exteriors are cached under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261009T181553786165-proto-support/ordered/rows/cache and may be read in place, never written. Run filepath relativize over any evidence fragment before committing. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step and write the manifest and commit before every job wait; the manifest commits line lists every commit; status is complete, blocked or failed, which the worker sets itself. No plan labels in source names or comments.\n\nImport provenance: run each arm from its own tree as the working directory and print nova.__file__ in each log header. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), run CPU gates in place, at most 8 at a time.",
